  "market_context": "Analyst identified a major HTF structure level on EUR/USD 1H that had acted as support and resistance multiple times. Price entered the supply area, then formed a double top on the 5M chart with neckline break.",
  "key_observation": "A double top formed on the 5-minute chart after price reacted at a major higher-timeframe structure level; neckline break confirmed reversal, enabling a precise 0.618 Fibonacci retracement sell limit entry.",
  "analysis_steps": [
    "Step 1: Identify a major higher-timeframe structure level on EUR/USD 1H that has rejected price multiple times and recently acted as both support and resistance.",
    "Step 2: Zoom into the 5-minute chart and observe price entering the supply area near that HTF level, then forming a double top pattern with two swing highs and a neckline connecting the intervening low.",
    "Step 3: Confirm the double top by observing a break of the neckline to the downside.",
    "Step 4: Apply Fibonacci retracement from the start of the impulsive move (swing low before double top) to the end (second swing high), placing a sell limit order at the 0.618 level.",
    "Step 5: Set stop-loss above the second swing high (highest point of the double top), and target the next lower market structure level for >1:2 risk-to-reward."
  ],
  "outcome": null,
  "lessons": "Combining double top/bottom patterns with Fibonacci retracement improves entry precision and risk management; always anchor such setups to significant higher-timeframe structure levels for higher-probability trades.",
